== Join Us
Prospective graduate students with strong interests in both physical chemistry and
the planets are encouraged to get in touch by email. Applications go through the
[https://www.stonybrook.edu/geosciences/graduate/programs/ Department of Geosciences].

Prospective postdocs in mineral physics, petrology, geophysics, planetary
science, or astrophysics are also welcome to contact me. Please send a CV
and the names of your references. Fellowships such as the NASA Hubble
Fellowship are another good route.

Experiment and theory each have a life of their own. In our group, we try
our best to live in both: experimentalists learn some theory, and
theorists go to the beamline and learn the instruments. Science has always
grown from many places and traditions, so anyone who shares our
curiosity and questions is welcome here. I meet regularly with each
student and postdoc, and I support travel to beamtime and conferences.
